  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760020,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 187: Ride or Die - PlayStation 2\n\nStep into the gritty streets of Los Angeles' South Central in *187: Ride or Die*, a high-octane racing game for the PlayStation 2. Developed and published by Ubisoft, this isn't your typical racing experience. Forget sprawling open worlds; *187* delivers intense, competitive races where vehicular combat is key to becoming the \"top dog.\"\n\nThe game pits you against rival racers in a series of events that blend traditional racing with aggressive gunplay. Your car is your weapon – strategically utilize mounted guns to disable opponents while striving to cross the finish line. Each race presents a unique challenge, alternating between pure speed and outright destruction. \n\nWhile clearly inspired by the popularity of *Grand Theft Auto*, *187* distinguishes itself with its focused racing gameplay. It's a fast-paced, arcade-style experience designed for adrenaline-fueled competition. Be warned, though – critics weren't kind, citing issues with the game's overall execution. Still, *187: Ride or Die* offers a unique and chaotic twist on the racing genre."
    },
